# Story 10.1e live-validation artifacts — paired recompose ON/OFF scoring of run
# e5ed4b3a-fabb-46e6-8adb-5c1c0fc68889.
#
# COMMITTED: the adjudication images the verdict cites (`pairs_grid.jpg`, the per-shot
# `pair_sheets/*.jpg` for every discordant shot), every script, and every JSON that
# re-derives a number — screening.json, pairs.json, off.json, on.json, results.json,
# pairs_key.json, verdict.json, PREREGISTRATION.md, README.md.
#
# IGNORED: the raw 1920x1080 renders those sheets were built from —
#   off/    the incumbent arm, rebuilt by `run_pairs.py render-off` (ffmpeg only, no GPU,
#           ~2 minutes) against the committed pairs.json.
#   on/     the treatment arm, re-framed copies of the recompose output. Rebuilt by
#           `run_pairs.py render-on` — which needs ComfyUI started with
#           `--lowvram --cache-lru 10` and >=12 GiB free RAM, and costs roughly 1.2 h of
#           GPU time for 40 passes. Do NOT add `--disable-smart-memory`: 10.1e measured it
#           at 385-677 s/pass against 108 without it, and REQUIRED_FLAGS dropped it.
#   blind/  opaque-id copies of the two arms, rebuilt by `run_pairs.py score` in seconds
#           from off/ + on/ + the committed pairs_key.json.
#
# DO NOT BLANKET-DELETE. `workspace/e5ed4b3a-.../recomposed/` is the ONLY copy of the ON
# arm's source renders: `on/` holds re-framed derivatives, not originals, and rebuilding
# the sources means paying the GPU hour again. If you must clear space here, delete with an
# explicit exclusion — never `git clean`, which would also take the committed sheets'
# regeneration inputs and, in this directory's neighbours, has previously destroyed the
# only surviving copy of a render a human judged (see 10-1b-live-validation/.gitignore).

off/
on/
blind/
score_progress.jsonl

# Viewing package (10.1e, for the human gate the scored axis does not cover).
# COMMITTED: viewing.json (what was built, what is excluded, the read-once notes) and the
#   identity_*.jpg sheets — those are adjudication images and survive at ~256px per cell.
# IGNORED: the side-by-side motion clips. ~8 MB, and rebuilt in about a minute with
#   `run_pairs.py viewing` (ffmpeg only, NO GPU) from off/ + on/, which are themselves
#   rebuilt by `render-off` / `render-on`. Keep off/ and on/ before deleting these.
viewing/*.mp4
